A revoke that takes the first child out of the ring without handing up its children
leaves them linked up to an empty slot, out of the root's reach.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: link up to a slot that is not a live, filled one
Witness: fuzz actor-handoff

diff --git a/kernel/cap.c b/kernel/cap.c
--- a/kernel/cap.c
+++ b/kernel/cap.c
@@ -279,7 +279,7 @@ bool cap_revoke_below(struct cap *root, uint32_t through, bool preempt)
 bool cap_delete(struct cap *n, bool preempt)
 {
     if (cap_next(n) != LINK_UP) {
-        detach(n, true);
+        detach(n, false);
         clear_node(n);
         return true;
     }
